# {{ project_name }} Architecture

> Hand-maintained, not generated. `just ci-arch` fails CI if a top-level module/package under
> `src/{{ python_package_name }}/` has no matching section here, or no box in the Component
> Diagram — see `AGENTS.md` "Architecture documentation". Diagrams are plain ASCII/Unicode
> box-drawing text in an untagged fenced code block, not Mermaid — a diagram you can update in
> the same PR as the code, not a separate rendering step.
>
> The views follow the [C4 model](https://c4model.com/) levels (which is notation-independent,
> so plain text is a valid rendering) and [arc42](https://arc42.org/overview)'s view names:
>
> | Section | C4 level | arc42 view |
> |---|---|---|
> | System Overview | Context + Container | §3 Context and Scope, §6 Runtime View |
> | Component Diagram | Component | §5 Building Block View, level 1 |
> | A component's own diagram | Code (only where it earns it) | §5 Building Block View, level 2 |
>
> Every diagram: a one-line title saying what it shows, one notation throughout, and a label on
> any arrow whose meaning isn't obvious (`──reads──▶`, `──HTTP──▶`).

